{"kind":"stack","id":"magnets-poles","title":"Magnets have 2 poles","theme":{"background":"#fff8e7","foreground":"#1f2937","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Magnetic poles"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"Every magnet has two ends called poles, north and south. The strongest pull is found at the poles."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1-next","kind":"flash","elements":[],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Like poles repel"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Two north poles push each other away. Two south poles push each other away too."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"How many poles does a bar magnet have?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Two","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"One","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Four","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"What happens when two north poles are brought together?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"They pull together","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"They push apart","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Nothing happens","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"Your magnet is lost in a cupboard. Do you search the shelf or the drawer?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Search the shelf","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5-shelf"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Search the drawer","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5-drawer"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5-shelf","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-shelf-t","content":"You find the magnet on the shelf. Its north and south poles help you pick up a paper clip."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-shelf-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5-drawer","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-drawer-t","content":"You find the magnet in the drawer, stuck to a metal spoon at one of its poles."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-drawer-next","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"Where is a magnet's pull strongest?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"At the poles","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"In the middle","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-c","label":"Evenly all over","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-q","content":"Which pair of poles will attract, or pull together?"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a","label":"North and south","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"North and north","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-c","label":"South and south","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"A magnet is cut in half. How many poles does each half have?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Two","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"One","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"None","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which of these is a pole of a magnet?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"The north end","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"The paint on its side","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"The wooden box it sits in","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-h","content":"Well done! You finished the magnets lesson."},{"type":"text","id":"c10-m","content":"Magnets have two poles, north and south. Keep exploring!"}],"actions":[]}}
